{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: contract amendment 4 revision 2 at 53537a58559861905b1b050487fcfd5f7f22341b, resting on all six artifacts with docs/protocol.md first. This approves the amendment and its compiling contract/UI/CLI integration only, as condition 4 requires. Publication, Room storage, verification and recovery implementation still require their separate deliveries and the normative acceptance cases.\n\nAll three changes requested in review 2e38de90 are addressed in the design. Any oversized entry—including an old sealed but unpublished entry—is published through authenticated chunked bytes, without changing its canonical bytes, hash or signature. Logical event, policy/checker and audience caps are removed; notifications, revert scopes, policy activations and recomputed obligations remain complete. Recursive directory fan-out addresses concentration under a retained digest prefix and growth in segment/entry/chunk collections. Every pushed commit remains durably outstanding until confirmed or fenced out by a forward ref movement; refusal of a retry, parent read-back, token expiry and revocation do not erase the earlier unknown attempt.\n\nArchitecture: signed Checkpoint.layout fixes version 2 and from at the first confirmed layout-2 commit. Before that, each candidate derives from its own parent, so confirming a late layout-1 commit correctly changes the next switch candidate's boundary. Closed segment bytes stay unchanged; legacy oversized confirmed segments are reused by ID. The new object layout has deterministic byte closing, chunk naming and directory placement, while preserving the entry format, root and old layout-1 verification. The 8 MiB blob bound and 4,096-entry directory bound leave ample margin against the dated measured 32 MiB object limit. The pre-storage guard covers newly written objects; reused legacy object IDs are explicitly exempt. Required lane edits explain the outstanding-commit store, classifier, streaming/chunked storage, decoder/verifier and rollout order.\n\nSecurity: a ChunkedLine binds byte length, digest and seq; verification reassembles the exact bytes, checks that binding, then verifies the entry's own hash/signature and normal authority/policy rules. Retained inputs/policies remain authenticated by digest at their deterministic paths. R-LOG-20 preserves unresolved push identity and relies on compare-and-swap leases on a monotonically advancing log ref. Under that declared single-writer boundary, two candidates on the same parent cannot both apply. Foreign writers still stop publication. Diagnostic ref movements in a local Git repository confirmed both legal orderings: C wins/D loses its lease, and D wins/C loses its lease. This checks the underlying CAS behavior, not an implementation of the future Room recovery engine.\n\nSimplification: one chunking rule and one fan-out rule replace many special size caps and dropped-event fallbacks. The distinct refused, object-too-large, unexpected-writer and unresolved reasons give useful admin state; UI text now distinguishes a halted foreign-writer case from retry behavior. Readers/decoders/classifier must ship before any Room writes layout 2.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci installed 374 packages; root strict typecheck passed, UI 141 and CLI 102 tests passed. Read all six artifacts and the complete revised protocol section. Their paths exactly match changes against base b5864882; no other candidate source changed against that base. Independent reference-function controls passed for exact-B closure, the next byte, 1,000-entry closure, an already-confirmed oversized legacy segment, the old B+1 unpublished entry, B+1/20 MiB chunk lengths, deep shared-prefix retained sharding and 5,000 segment names. In the prior failing example [10, B+1] with from:1, the logical large line now occupies a 120-byte marker in segment 0, with chunks of 8,388,608 and 1 bytes. The pathological 5,000-retained-file prefix terminates with 256 names per leaf; the largest leaf tree is bounded by 397,312 bytes. No live deployment, model call, credential use or remote push was performed. The worktree is clean.\n\nNonblocking wording follow-up: R-LOG-18 says ChunkedLine has no key that an entry has, but both have seq. Say it has the reserved chunked form and lacks an entry's type/normal fields; require exact-form decoding. The measured Artifacts constant's comment should retain its dated namespace/probe scope rather than imply an undocumented universal service guarantee.\n\nFull-scope follow-up: open point 41 explicitly leaves transport reads of very large entries undefined. It remains necessary work for complete API/subscribe usability, not a functional limit on what the Room may seal or publish and not something removed to meet an estimate. Implementations must make those reads consumable within transport limits. Preserve the full large-notification/revert/activation acceptance cases and separately track this read interface.\n\nDiagnostics: /tmp/artroom-checker-log-Am4-v2-diagnostics/layout.mjs, layout-results.txt, cas-results.json. Type/UI/CLI gates: /tmp/artroom-checker-log-Am4-v2-*. No new runtime publisher or live large-object result is credited by this contract approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25a1c240c859e26d1af6490c1fedd2efaa0bd04f","binding":"assigned","head":"53537a58559861905b1b050487fcfd5f7f22341b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5e183da72547ac3775ddd54a32e5cd5b1982a852\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f50fb7f7e1eda79085341fe5fd198d7f6c8e89c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5e183da72547ac3775ddd54a32e5cd5b1982a852","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}